  "hindi": "हे वरुण, तेरे व्रत में हम सौभाग्यशाली हों, भक्त और स्तुति करनेवाले होकर, गायों से युक्त उषाओं के आगमन पर, अग्नियों के समान प्रतिदिन स्तुति करते हुए।",
  "english": "May we be fortunate in your ordinance, O Varuṇa, devout and having praised you, at the approach of the cow-rich dawns, praising day after day like fires.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "Printed 'upāyana' is read as upāyane (loc.) before the vowel of uṣasām (Vedic e before a vowel appears as a); no error assumed. 'svādhyaḥ' is taken as su-ādhyaḥ, devout, thoughtful. 'jaramāṇāḥ' could also be taken as 'crackling' for the fires; here taken as 'praising'. 'anu dyūn' read as 'day after day'.",
  "confidence": "medium"
 },
