  "hindi": "हे वरुण, हे नायक, बहुत वीरों से युक्त और दूर तक प्रशंसित तेरे आश्रय में हम रहें। हे अदिति के पुत्रो, हे अपराजित देवो, तुम हमारे साथ मित्रता के लिए क्षमाशील बनो।",
  "english": "O Varuṇa, O leader, may we be in the shelter of you who have many heroes and are widely praised. O sons of Aditi, O undeceived gods, be forbearing towards us for fellowship.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "'yūyaṃ naḥ' could also be read 'you, ours'; taken as 'you ... towards us'. 'abhi kṣamadhvam' is rendered 'be forbearing towards (us)'; the exact sense of abhi-√kṣam here is uncertain. 'adabdhāḥ' literally 'not to be deceived/harmed'. The first line reads as a wish with tava ... śarman: 'in your shelter'.",
  "confidence": "medium"
 },
