  "hindi": "आदित्य ने, धारण करनेवाले ने, इन्हें आगे छोड़ा है; नदियाँ वरुण के ऋत की ओर जाती हैं। ये न थकती हैं, न रुकती हैं; पक्षियों के समान तेजी से अपने परिक्रमा-पथ पर उड़ चली हैं।",
  "english": "Āditya the upholder has sent them forth; the rivers go along the order of Varuṇa. These do not tire and do not stop; like birds they have flown swiftly on their circuit.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "Printed 'vidhartā~' (with a nasal sign) is not certain: taken as vidhartā, nominative, with the nasal a sandhi or editorial mark. 'sīm' taken as 'them' (the rivers). 'ṛtam yanti' literally 'go (to/along) the order'. 'paptū' in 'papta' is paptuḥ with visarga lost before r (paptū raghuyā). 'parijman' taken as loc. 'on the circuit/round'.",
